Verizon Communications Inc. reported the highest 2022 revenue of $136.8 billion, which is greater than the revenues of Coca‑Cola and AES (their 2022 revenues were not provided in the data).  The company’s 2022 Form 10‑K identifies its main risk factors as:
• Potentially significant costs or reduced benefits from network enhancements;
• Inability to implement its business strategy;
• Adverse economic conditions and inflation in the U.S. and international markets;
• Cyber‑attack threats that could disrupt its networks or cause financial and reputational damage.
